class.description:
A resource that decides whether a state machine transition is taken. Extend it in a script and implement [method _check]. It is saved inside the [HierarchicalStateMachine] file, on the [member HSMTransition.condition] of a row.
On a polled transition (empty event), the condition is asked on every update while the origin state is active. On an event transition, it acts as an extra guard asked when the event arrives.
A [HierarchicalStateMachine] resource is usually shared by many machines. A [LimboHSM] that builds from it duplicates each condition and binds the copy to itself, so [member blackboard], [member agent] and [member machine] belong to that machine and any state the script keeps between checks is per machine. The condition stored in the resource is never bound or modified at runtime.
[codeblock]
@tool
extends HSMCondition

@export var variable: StringName = &"in_combat"

func _generate_name() -> String:
    return "Var %s" % variable

func _check() -> bool:
    return blackboard.get_var(variable, false)
[/codeblock]
